From eaf8ae7e0ff7848f9a5dda63437bf3347e4eb955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:41:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 156/156] wifi: mt6797: install and retire the WPA2 keys in the
 firmware

Phase C2 lets the standard supplicant finish the four-way handshake. Key
ownership follows the pinned vendor implementation: each key the
supplicant installs becomes one CMD_ID_ADD_REMOVE_KEY (0x07) on the TC4
owner, the 64-byte CMD_802_11_KEY as wlanoidSetAddKey fills it for a
WPA2-PSK CCMP station (add, TX key and unicast type for the pairwise
key, neither for the group key, the AP's address as the peer for both,
BSS 0, CIPHER_SUITE_CCMP, the key id, 16 bytes, WLAN index 1 or the
declared BMC index 0) and, at the end, as wlanoidSetRemoveKey fills a
removal (the zeroed command with the key id, peer, BSS and, for the
pairwise key, unicast type and WLAN index). The RSC is zero in both, as
the pinned wlanoidSetAddKey zeroes the command and never writes it for
CCMP. A join whose association request carried the admitted RSN
element declares AUTH_MODE_WPA2_PSK and ENUM_ENCRYPTION3_ENABLED in its
BSS payload, as the vendor does at connect time.

set_key submits one pairwise key then one group key (key id 0 to 3),
CCMP only, for the exact peer, with the same credit wait as the join
commands; a returned credit proves only that the firmware consumed the
command and the records say submitted and credit returned. The
standard supplicant hands message 4 to the driver before installing the
pairwise key, so set_key first waits for an in-flight reply's TX done
and credit on the existing ledger, and a reply that is only queued
stays queued while the command's page is owed. The group key's credit
shortens the deauthentication hold to one second. DISABLE_KEY submits
nothing. Anything else ends the lifetime fail-stop. Key material lives
only in mac80211's key, the command payload and the transfer buffer,
each cleared after submission; no record carries a key byte.

On the healthy path the cleanup removes each submitted key with its
own bounded command, pairwise first, after the deauthentication has
completed and before the station removal, channel abort and BSS-off
stages, because the pinned source does not show that removing the
station record retires the group key held under the BMC index.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
